**WorkPulse** is a multi-company construction operations app. It is for **managers and team leads**, not a public website: you pick a company, see only that company’s crews, sites, stock, and daily work, then fill what got done.

The product idea is: **one site (a project) can be run two ways at once** — a Jira-style task board, and a daily sheet of amounts — and both write the same daily reports.

Phase 1 (branch `phase1-site-ops`) grew that into a site-operations core: who was on site each day, a daily log that a manager approves and locks, progress with forecasts and team performance, stock tied to the work it was used for, and photo/PDF uploads.

---

## What it is, in one picture

```text
Company (River Co, own time zone)
  ├── People: teams, workers, optional leads
  │     └── Team membership history (who was in which team, when)
  ├── Catalogs: work kinds, measures (m²/m³), work types, statuses, phases, duration units
  │     └── Material norms per work type (1.4 kg adhesive per m² of facade)
  ├── Projects (sites / workplaces)
  │     ├── Teams placed on the site, with dates
  │     ├── Scopes (work type + planned quantity)
  │     ├── Tasks (board / timeline)
  │     ├── Sheet columns (how the table is set up)
  │     ├── Site reports (what was done on a day)
  │     ├── Crew attendance (which workers were on site on a day)
  │     ├── Daily logs (one per day: notes, weather, issues, approval)
  │     └── Material requests (site asks the depot for stock)
  ├── Stock: depot + site locations, lots, movements, minimum levels
  └── Attachments: photos and PDFs on any record
```

A **report** is the core fact: *this team, on this project, on this date, on this work type, did this quantity*. Progress is the sum of those reports. The sheet is just a grid over the same reports. The board is tasks that can be linked to a report.

**The rule that holds it together:** every fact is a row that gets added, and every number on a screen is a sum of those rows. Phase 1 added new kinds of fact, never a second copy of an old one:

| Fact | Table | Numbers built from it |
|------|-------|-----------------------|
| Work done | `SiteReport` | Progress, remaining, weekly output, forecast finish |
| Crew on site | `CrewAttendance` | Worker-days, output per worker-day |
| Material moved or used | `StockMovement` | Stock on hand, use per work type, expected vs actual |
| Day signed off | `DailyLog` | Which days are locked |

