## How code is organized

### Repository layout

```text
workpulse/
  docker-compose.yml
  backend/          Django project
    config/         settings, urls, pagination
    accounts/       login, register, session, /me
    companies/      Company (+ timezone), Membership, roles, seed_demo
    workforce/      Team, Worker, TeamMembership, move_worker, active_on
    operations/     projects, catalogs, reports, sheet, placements
      progress.py   pace, forecasts, team performance, portfolio
    work/           tasks, board statuses/phases
    sitelog/        DailyLog, issues, crew attendance, day lock
    inventory/      stock, norms, stock levels, material requests
      usage.py      expected vs actual material, shortages
    core/           activity feed, attachments
  frontend/         CRA React 19
    src/pages/      one route ≈ one screen
    src/components/ reusable UI (board, sheet, calendar, day log, charts)
    src/context/    auth + theme
    src/api/        fetch wrapper
```

### Backend pattern (repeated in every app)

| File | Job |
|------|-----|
| `models.py` | Tables and constraints |
| `services.py` | Rules: create defaults, prepare report, upsert sheet cell, remaining, day lock, move worker |
| `serializers.py` | Validate + shape JSON |
| `views.py` / `viewsets.py` | HTTP: thin, call services |
| `urls.py` | Mount under `/api/` |
| `tests.py` | API tests with a logged-in client |

Views inherit `CompanyScopedViewSet`: filter by company, set company on create, turn `ProtectedError` into 400 instead of a crash.

Business logic stays in **services**, not in the view. Example: filling a report goes `ViewSet → Serializer.validate → prepare_site_report → create`. `prepare_site_report` checks the day is open and the team is placed on that date. Duplicate team+date+scope becomes a validation error, including on a race (`IntegrityError`).

### Frontend pattern

- **Pages** pick data and layout (`ProjectPage` has tabs: Overview, Board, Sheet, Timeline, Teams, Daily log, Stock).
- **New pages:** `PlanningPage` (`/planning`), `TeamPage` (`/teams/:id`), `WorkerPage` (`/workers/:id`).
- **Components** own a feature: `WorkSheet`, `DailyReports` + `ReportCalendar`, `DayLog`, `TaskBoard`, `TaskTimeline`, `ProjectProgress`, `SiteMaterials`, `MaterialUseForm`, `MaterialNorms`, `StockLevels`, `MaterialRequestsQueue`, `AttachmentGrid`.
- **Charts** are small inline-SVG components in `charts.js`; no chart library.
- **`ui.js`** is shared primitives (page header, fields, tabs) using CSS variables.
- Sidebar: Work has **Daily log** (was Reports) and **Planning**. Managers see Work types / Workflow; leads do not.

Calendar is shared: Daily log and Sheet both use `ReportCalendar` (day / week / month, today, marked dates).

